itch terminology in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rust-core-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rust-core-contract: add canonical Rust domain names and parser/wire [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]compatibility while preserving serialized and binding contracts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate the Python domain and ProjectSpec storage layer[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]python-domain-storage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rust-core-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]python-domain-storage: introduce canonical models, modules, parsing, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]formatting, persistence, and wire adapters with legacy aliases.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rename workflow, automation, CLI, and metadata contracts[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]workflows-cli-contracts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after python-domain-storage[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]workflows-cli-contracts: migrate lifecycle, automation, command, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine-facing call sites while keeping old entry points and data [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]compatible.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rename the ACE TUI and configuration surface[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-config-surface[dim] · [dim][/dim]after workflows-cli-contracts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-config-surface: present Patches and stitches throughout ACE and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]normalize legacy keymap, config, completion, and saved-state [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identifiers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Update linked GitHub, Telegram, and Neovim integrations[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]linked-integrations[dim] · [dim][/dim]after workflows-cli-contracts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]linked-integrations: adopt canonical APIs and labels in GitHub, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Telegram, and Neovim while retaining mixed-version compatibility.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Update documentation, glossary, demos, and generated-skill [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]sources[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-memory-skills[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui-config-surface, linked-integrations[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-memory-skills: rewrite maintained explanatory surfaces, regenerate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory shims, and prepare generated skills from authoritative sources.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile compatibility and verify the complete rename[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]compatibility-audit[dim] · [dim][/dim]after docs-memory-skills[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]compatibility-audit: classify every remaining legacy token and run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exhaustive cross-repository compatibility and regression verification.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-hn","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-hn.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e5dce70d4635dac3c7c0acd3c52a4687","started_at":"2026-08-08T17:08:16.272369+00:00","state":"active"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.6","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.7","bbugyi200.athena.sase-hn.land"]}
